No extensions directory available — proceeding with the analysis using the core + extended catalog. Here is the full formal audit.

---

## testsmells.org 19-Smell Academic Audit

**Target:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` — MSTest 4.1, .NET 10, `[TestCategory("Integration")]`

### 1. Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Total    | **4**       | **4**          |

4 of 8 test methods are clean.

---

### 2. Findings by Severity

#### ❌ HIGH — Sleepy Test (Smell #3)

**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);  // blocks thread for 3 seconds
```

Even in integration tests, `Thread.Sleep` is a smell: it introduces non-determinism (3 s may be too short on slow CI, always too long on fast machines) and slows the suite. The method is also declared `async Task` but uses a synchronous sleep, wasting the async signature.

**Fix — use polling or async wait with timeout:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    // Poll with timeout instead of a fixed sleep
    var timeout = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5);
    var interval = TimeSpan.FromMilliseconds(100);
    var sw = Stopwatch.StartNew();
    while (!_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
    {
        Assert.IsTrue(sw.Elapsed < timeout, "Notification was not sent within timeout.");
        await Task.Delay(interval);
    }
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky CI failures, artificially slow test suite.

---

#### ❌ HIGH — Conditional Test Logic (Smell #1)

**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 101-108)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

One branch will **never execute** (a regular `Insert` won't produce a `PremiumUser`), giving the illusion of coverage on a dead path. The two branches test entirely different properties, hiding which behavior is actually verified.

**Fix — split into two deterministic tests:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    var user = new User("eve@example.com", "Eve");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetPremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    var user = new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.1m);
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com")!;

    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Hidden testing gap — the `PremiumUser` branch is likely dead code that never runs.

---

#### ❌ HIGH — Assertion-Free Test / Unknown Test (Smell #4)

**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113-119)

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // No assertion — passes as long as no exception is thrown
}
```

The test name suggests "runs without errors" (implicit no-throw assertion), but this gives false confidence: a silently corrupted write would still pass. MSTest will mark it green regardless of what the repository actually persisted.

**Fix — verify the observable outcome:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — the test cannot detect silent data corruption or partial inserts.

---

#### ⚠️ MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette (Extended Smell)

**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35-38)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

Four assertions, none with a message parameter. When one fails, the MSTest runner reports a line number but not *why* the assertion matters, making triage harder in CI logs.

**Fix — add message parameters:**

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip through persistence");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip through persistence");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Persisted user should have a positive auto-generated Id");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower triage when assertions fail in CI — minor but cumulative impact.

---

### 3. Smell-Free Patterns ✅

These 4 tests are well-structured:

| Test | Why it's good |
|------|---------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange-act-assert, focused assertions |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single precise null-check on the expected outcome |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count is self-documenting (3 inserts → 3 expected); uses `CollectionAssert` |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Good async pattern, verifies observable outcome |

The class also uses **in-memory SQLite** (`Data Source=:memory:`), which is a hermetic test strategy — no **Mystery Guest** smell despite the `[TestCategory("Integration")]` marker. Setup/teardown fields (`_connection`, `_repository`) are used by every test, so **General Fixture** does not apply either.

---

### 4. Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Test | Effort | Why first |
|----------|-------|------|--------|-----------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` | 🟢 Low — add one `Assert.AreEqual` | Eliminates a false-pass risk |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` | 🟡 Med — split into 2 tests | Eliminates a dead-code branch |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` | 🟡 Med — replace with polling loop | Removes flakiness and ~3 s of latency |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` | 🟢 Low — add message strings | Improves CI triage speed |

**Bottom line:** The suite's architecture (in-memory DB, proper lifecycle, focused test methods) is solid. Fix the 3 high-severity smells — especially the assertion-free test, which is a real false-pass risk — and this becomes a clean suite.
